# Golden templates — mandatory pointer

**Status: MANDATORY · NON-NEGOTIABLE.** Every new/edited Q&A page is exactly one of two immutable shapes.

**Read first, every session:** [`CURSOR_GOLDEN_TEMPLATES.md`](../../CURSOR_GOLDEN_TEMPLATES.md) — the self-contained Cursor Agent execution spec (router, session checklist, DEFAULTS, validation gate). Then read the sole shape law:

| Template | Spec | Gold ref |
|----------|------|----------|
| Top 10 ranking list | [`GOLDEN_TEMPLATE_TOP10.md`](../../GOLDEN_TEMPLATE_TOP10.md) | `aq1158` |
| Q&A essay | [`GOLDEN_TEMPLATE_QA.md`](../../GOLDEN_TEMPLATE_QA.md) | `q11133` |

No other golden-template markdown is authoritative.

## Rules

1. **Classify before generate** — `pickGoldTemplate(id, body, title)` in `_pulse_gold_template_router.js`, called before any draft/fix/audit/publish. Lock `template`, `goldId`, `goldUrl`, `reason` — **never switch mid-run**. Body shape wins over title wording.
2. **No hybrids** — exactly one template per entry; never merge `@@PRODUCT`/ranking pills into Q&A; never prepend a Q&A hero onto Top 10.
3. **13/13 gate only** — no publish below 13/13 on the content rubric (`SCRUBBER_SPEC.md`) + a clean gold audit (`auditQaGoldTemplate` / `auditTop10GoldTemplate`) + the full numbered §6/§7 checklist. No "12/13 close enough."
4. **Visual lock** — writers touch prose only; see `.cursor/rules/visual-lock-law.mdc`. Never touch images, `@@PRODUCT`, CRO, or schema from a text pass.
5. **Do not ask the user mid-run** — apply the DEFAULTS table in `CURSOR_GOLDEN_TEMPLATES.md`, then log the assumption to `logs/golden-template-assumptions.md`. Never block on a clarifying question.
6. **Validate spec-doc edits** — whenever `GOLDEN_TEMPLATE_QA.md` / `GOLDEN_TEMPLATE_TOP10.md` themselves change, run `node validate-golden.mjs --type qa|top10 <file>` and require exit 0 (13/13) before continuing.
7. **Bypass** — immutable shape law only, only with owner passcode **4444**; never for rubric, broken images, or gold-audit failures.

**Full detail lives in `CURSOR_GOLDEN_TEMPLATES.md` and the two golden specs — do not restate or fork template law here.**
